-effort lowercase name via `getattr(..., \"name\", \"\")`, returning `\"\"` (â†’ inert) if the engine build exposes no name attribute.\n  - `_sharpedo_conditional_bonus(card, attack, mon)` â€” returns the bonus **only** when the acting PokÃ©mon is a Mega Sharpedo ex (`card.megaEx` + name contains \"sharpedo\"), the attack is Hungry Jaws, **and** the PokÃ©mon is currently damaged (`mon.hp < mon.maxHp`). Every other PokÃ©mon/attack, and an undamaged Sharpedo, returns `0`.\n- Wired that bonus into the two damage-estimation paths the hypothesis names:\n  - **Immediate attacker scoring / lookahead eval:** `_best_usable_damage` (feeds `_live_attacker_score`, `_eval_state`) now adds the conditional bonus per affordable attack.\n  - **Attack choice:** `_best_attack_index` takes an optional acting `mon`; callers `_choose_main` (lethal check + fallback attack) and `_choose_attack` pass the current Active. This lets a damaged Sharpedo register lethal and rank Hungry Jaws correctly.\n\nGeneric ranking is untouched: `_card_power` (board development / evolve / play) was deliberately left alone, so Sharpedo's benched/undamaged value is not globally inflated.\n\n## Concerns for the human reviewer\n\n1. **Sign/direction risk (most important):** The fix assumes the engine's static `attack.damage` for Hungry Jaws is the **base** value (conditional not included). If instead the static table already stores the **boosted** value, this code double-counts on a damaged Sharpedo and the sign of any measured effect flips. Verify against the actual card DB before trusting results.\n2. **Bonus magnitude:** `HUNGRY_JAWS_CONDITIONAL_BONUS = 100` is my best estimate; confirm the real conditional amount from the card.\n3. **Name-attribute dependency:** Detection keys on a card/attack `.name` field. If this engine build doesn't expose names, the feature safely no-ops (behavior == baseline), which would make the experiment show a null effect rather than an error â€” worth confirming names are available so the test is actually exercised.\n\nI did not run any benchmarks or games, per the contract â€” the controller handles validation and games after exit.","ttft_ms":1641,"ttft_stream_ms":1527,"time_to_request_ms":245,"type":"result","duration_ms":218854,"uuid":"d9446a7c-cf3e-4638-98c9-7f3a43f64a6b"}
